    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132-a13">

                <pb facs="0233" n="153" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg153"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 8.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCaslin to Mr. Kristy.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Niuchwang</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Kristy</hi>: I am sorry to make a complaint
                    to you again. This time it is against the people who are docking the steam
                    launches. They started to-day to dig a dock on my ground next to the Russian
                    settlement.</p>
                <p>Anything they dock there they will have to pay for; each launch $600, and if the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Sampson</hi>, $1,000; then the expenses of filling
                    up the docks will have to be paid by the people who dug them.</p>
                <p>These docks will cause my land to wash away twice as fast as if they had not been
                    there.</p>
                <pb facs="0234" n="154" xml:id="pg154"/>
                <p>It seems to me as though some of the Russian people here think they can do what
                    they like with my land.</p>
                <p>I do not wish to make trouble, but they are going a little too far. If you will
                    notify the people who are digging the dock what they are doing, you will greatly
                    oblige.</p>
                <p>Yours, truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. McCaslin</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
